{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1031436-advice-on-a-antagonist-idea-for-mage","id":1031436,"title":"Advice on a antagonist idea for Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-13T20:29:14-08:00","id":1031436,"title":"Advice on a antagonist idea for Mage","content":"I have never played Mage before but I am considering buying it soon. In fact, I already came up with an antagonist for it. The Genesis Corporation. They are basically a corporation who want to clone human beings. The Traditionalists view them as a other cog in the Technocracy's machine while the Technocrats view them as a benevolent corporation with a noble goal. However, the corporation is secretly controlled by a Nephandi by the name of Curtis who serves The Outer Lords. My only question is would a nephandi be a chairman of a corporation and what the Nephandi could use human cloning for ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T20:48:23-08:00","id":1031442,"title":"","content":"The Nephandus would probably install a puppet chairman, as the Fallen tend to live longer when they aren't directly connected to their schemes. Even if it's a constructed identity, the Nephandus appearing as the chairman himself opens him to more risk, for little reward. A patsy, meanwhile, could be thrown under the bus if their master felt too much heat coming their way.<br /> <br /> How the cloning is used for Evil is an interesting question. Curtis could modify the genetic codes of the clones, so they had some kind of &quot;monster&quot; or &quot;killer&quot; gene implanted deep in their DNA. It could lie dormant for years, or even generations, before individuals manifest their effects at regular intervals (far enough apart that any rampages or the like wouldn't be easily tied to the company). The difficulty comes, of course, from the fact that Technocrats could spot such a thing if they cared to check the clones' DNA. A plot hook might revolve around a couple clones unexpectedly going rogue in a short timeframe, leading a Technocrat group to investigate the connection.<br /> <br /> Another, more subtle use, would be to make sure that all the clones are partially related to one individual. This, therefore, would mean they all share a Sympathetic (and therefore Correspondence) connection to a person in the Nephandus' control, if it isn't the Nephandus himself (though I doubt the Fallen would risk that same bond of Contagion being used against them). Suddenly, he has a legion of individuals that are predisposed towards being controlled by him magickally. Agents positioned in many places throughout society, susceptible to mind control or other Effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T20:53:23-08:00","id":1031443,"title":"","content":"Cloning is nothing new to the technocracy. The Progenitors have been doing it for decades, and pretty much the majority of grunts in the NWO are clones.<br /> In canon, cloning is not yet a part of the consensus, so it would be unlikely that the Technocracy would be ok with a company that wasn't theirs pulling this kind of stuff off.<br /> <br /> But perhaps things are a bit different in your game. Perhaps the technocracy have approached a part of their timetable where cloning is due to become part of the consensus, and now they're getting Syndicate managed enterprises in place to start normalising cloning, having as many people accept it as possible and turn it into consensus.<br /> <br /> This is the perfect environment for a nephandic group to reign some terror.<br /> <br /> If he serves an outer lord, then they'd be a K'lasshaa. These guys tend to be more solitary than the others. A single mad man who carries out their dark pleasures for the sake of forces beyond our comprehension. A rich eccentric type who owned a few companies would be a good fit for this. Perhaps they even used to be a Syndicate technoctrat before the became one of the fallen.<br /> <br /> Why would they do it? Who's to say. Perhaps their outer god craves sacrifices, and this is the easiest way to make a steady supply of them without garnering too much suspicion. Perhaps the cloning centre is a front for more questionable biological activity designed to create monsters in their outer god's image. Perhaps they just get a kick out of having a never ending supply of human victims for their rituals.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, they could be A Malfean Nephandi in service to the Wyrm, and their cloning company is a offshoot of Pentex inc. a company run exclusively by Wyrm tainted beings both spiritual and mundane. If you're familiar with Werewolf the Apocolypse, this might be a more natural option for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T21:14:50-08:00","id":1031444,"title":"","content":"You know, I was considering making their Nephandi master a Malfean. Also, I was thinking about the company being founded after the mundane founder, a Indian scientist by the name of Jahnu Narang got into a argument with his former employer, DNA. Before quitting DNA, Jahnu was hired by DNA to beachhead their cloning research program. Unfortunately, near that time DNA found out about GLS and cut most of the funding to the cloning program in favor for studying GLS. Jahnu, understandably, was pissed. He thought DNA made up GLS as a excuse to cut funding from his already expensive project. So, in his fury, he quit DNA and took much of his research staff and research notes and started the Genesis Corporation. The Nephandi comes in shortly afterwards and offers to invest money in this corporation in exchange for 50% of the company's stock. Jahnu, of course, agrees.<br /> <br /> Also, don't think the mundane employees and executives are innocent joes. In fact, some of them can be even more sadistic than the Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T22:45:10-08:00","id":1031463,"title":"","content":"Another possibility would be for the Mage to be an Infernal Technocrat instead of a Nephandi. He would be secretly using Dark Technology to create clones that will be inclined to sin in the fashion associated with his patron. He might even be a Technocrat in good standing who gained permission to introduce a commercial version of reproductive cloning to prepare the Masses for more advanced cloning technology to come in the next couple of decades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T00:54:43-08:00","id":1031493,"title":"","content":"My first thought was that the clones create another social class, above or below the old fashioned humans.<br /> E.g. the Nephandus aims for legal human rights violations, because cloned humans are \u201cdifferent\u201c.<br /> Cheap workers(comparatively, the upbringing doesn't cost the company but the community).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T08:23:11-08:00","id":1031594,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about having the company not being successful in cloning a full human yet. But, the experiments they have succeeded in is the cloning of animals like apes, ala Dolly the sheep. They think they are on the verge of a breakthrough in their program. Also, the company's biggest opponent in the Traditions would be either The Celestial Chorus or The Verbena. Also, I guess the Progenitors would hate them too.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, fighting their human employees would be tough due to the fact you can't use magic on them due to paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T10:12:13-08:00","id":1031643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1031436-advice-on-a-antagonist-idea-for-mage?p=1031594#post1031594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAlso, fighting their human employees would be tough due to the fact you can't use magic on them due to paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as the magic is subtle, i.e. coincidental, you can do whatever you like in front of a Sleeper with relative assurance that paradox will not be a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T10:17:56-08:00","id":1031649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1031436-advice-on-a-antagonist-idea-for-mage?p=1031643#post1031643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As long as the magic is subtle, i.e. coincidental, you can do whatever you like in front of a Sleeper with relative assurance that paradox will not be a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI found that out while looking trough the White Wolf wiki. Also, what do you think of the connection between Genesis and DNA. Also, I am still debating making their Nephandi boss a Malfean or K'lasshaa. Can you see the Celestial Chorus, Verbena and Progenitors hating them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T10:38:00-08:00","id":1031668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1031436-advice-on-a-antagonist-idea-for-mage?p=1031649#post1031649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI found that out while looking trough the White Wolf wiki. Also, what do you think of the connection between Genesis and DNA. Also, I am still debating making their Nephandi boss a Malfean or K'lasshaa. Can you see the Celestial Chorus, Verbena and Progenitors hating them?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll have to clarify, do you mean Biblical Genesis and Molecular DNA? Or do you mean your two fictional companies Genesis and DNA?<br /> <br /> As for the Nephandi. Everyone hates the nephandi. One of the most revered Protocols of the Council of Nine is &quot;Conspire Not with the Enemies of Ascension&quot;. Nephandi are the very definition of enemies of ascension, and would be detested on all sides as a general rule.<br /> The Chorus consider them to be doing the work of the devil. The Verbena see them as a disgusting force of pollution and corruption, and the Progenitors would think of them as a cancer which is best removed.<br /> <br /> Now, when dealing with individuals you can afford to be a lot more nuanced and layered in the way each mage considers the others, perhaps they might even sympathise with the nephandi (though stating such in the wrong company would be tantamount to suicide). Some may even think &quot;K'lashaa? Oh yeah, they're dangerous, but no where near as vile as the Malfeans&quot;. Others might not even be aware there's a difference, or even care. &quot;They want to destroy everything. Why bother with their reasoning? Just kill 'em!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T10:41:04-08:00","id":1031671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1031436-advice-on-a-antagonist-idea-for-mage?p=1031668#post1031668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'll have to clarify, do you mean Biblical Genesis and Molecular DNA? Or do you mean your two fictional companies Genesis and DNA?<br /> <br /> As for the Nephandi. Everyone hates the nephandi. One of the most revered Protocols of the Council of Nine is &quot;Conspire Not with the Enemies of Ascension&quot;. Nephandi are the very definition of enemies of ascension, and would be detested on all sides as a general rule.<br /> The Chorus consider them to be doing the work of the devil. The Verbena see them as a disgusting force of pollution and corruption, and the Progenitors would think of them as a cancer which is best removed.<br /> <br /> Now, when dealing with individuals you can afford to be a lot more nuanced and layered in the way each mage considers the others, perhaps they might even sympathise with the nephandi (though stating such in the wrong company would be tantamount to suicide). Some may even think &quot;K'lashaa? Oh yeah, they're dangerous, but no where near as vile as the Malfeans&quot;. Others might not even be aware there's a difference, or even care. &quot;They want to destroy everything. Why bother with their reasoning? Just kill 'em!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBy DNA I meant the company in Werewolf the Apocalypse. Also, I meant how would those Mage groups would view the Genesis Corporation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T13:05:17-08:00","id":1031756,"title":"","content":"The Progenitors are going to be very interested in how a corporation that isn't under their wing has such advanced technology. They are going to investigate, and if everything they do follows the canon of established mundane science, they are going to be very happy, and may offer assistance. But if it smells as pseudoscience they aren't going to like it, they might even be hostile to the corporation.<br /> <br /> The Choristers might think it as a souless corporation that toys with human life without caring about the spirit. Although that depends a bit on how Genesis sells themselves.<br /> The average chorister it's going to hate it if they present themselves as an atheistic ultratech industry &quot;improving god's design&quot;, and if it only offers beneffits for rich people or if it treats it's clones as souless labor force, or as body replacements for dead people.<br /> They might be more open if the institution is humble about what they're doing, and talk about improving life for everyone. But they ain't likely to cherish the institution anyway.<br /> <br /> The Verbena are going to see it as a perversion of nature. They might hate it even more if they present themselves as &quot;improving nature's design&quot; (you may see a pattern here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), but they are going to hate it no matter how well they market themselves.<br /> The Verbena hate humanity forcing the cicles of life. Replacing natural birth with machines it's like a slapt to the face of their paradigm. Nothing it's going to diminish their rage.<br /> <br /> They both WILL think it's a Technocratic front . They might organize protests and try to shut down the place (trough influence or sabotage), but, since they will think it's a Technocratic institution, they might be too scared of retaliation to confront the corporation in a direct way, unless they're very strong, or very bold. (Player characters are going to run against it with torches, if they're like some of my group. But that's another matter :P ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-14-2017, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T13:22:21-08:00","id":1031768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1031436-advice-on-a-antagonist-idea-for-mage?p=1031756#post1031756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Progenitors are going to be very interested in how a corporation that isn't under their wing has such advanced technology. They are going to investigate, and if everything they do follows the canon of established mundane science, they are going to be very happy, and may offer assistance. But if it smells as pseudoscience they aren't going to like it, they might even be hostile to the corporation.<br /> <br /> The Choristers might think it as a souless corporation that toys with human life without caring about the spirit. Although that depends a bit on how Genesis sells themselves.<br /> The average chorister it's going to hate it if they present themselves as an atheistic ultratech industry &quot;improving god's design&quot;, and if it only offers beneffits for rich people or if it treats it's clones as souless labor force, or as body replacements for dead people.<br /> They might be more open if the institution is humble about what they're doing, and talk about improving life for everyone. But they ain't likely to cherish the institution anyway.<br /> <br /> The Verbena are going to see it as a perversion of nature. They might hate it even more if they present themselves as &quot;improving nature's design&quot; (you may see a pattern here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), but they are going to hate it no matter how well they market themselves.<br /> The Verbena hate humanity forcing the cicles of life. Replacing natural birth with machines it's like a slapt to the face of their paradigm. Nothing it's going to diminish their rage.<br /> <br /> They both WILL think it's a Technocratic front . They might organize protests and try to shut down the place (trough influence or sabotage), but, since they will think it's a Technocratic institution, they might be too scared of retaliation to confront the corporation in a direct way, unless they're very strong, or very bold. (Player characters are going to run against it with torches, if they're like some of my group. But that's another matter :P ).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe mundane founder, Jahnu Narang, claims that Genesis' ultimate goal is humanities' immortality through cloning. Though, they haven't been able to clone a human yet. Some of their other goals is cloning human organs and cloning extinct animals ala Jurassic Park. I wonder how the rest of the Traditions and Conventions would view them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T14:53:00-08:00","id":1031831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1031436-advice-on-a-antagonist-idea-for-mage?p=1031768#post1031768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThe mundane founder, Jahnu Narang, claims that Genesis' ultimate goal is humanities' immortality through cloning. Though, they haven't been able to clone a human yet. Some of their other goals is cloning human organs and cloning extinct animals ala Jurassic Park. I wonder how the rest of the Traditions and Conventions would view them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Euthanatos are going to have a big bone to pick with them due to their goals clashing hard with their 8 spoked wheel, the Chodona. Immortality denies Kala, the belief that all things will and must decay in time, and return to the other side of the cycle. While Gopaya compels them to act against anything which may corrupt the cycle of Death and Rebirth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T15:07:08-08:00","id":1031836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1031436-advice-on-a-antagonist-idea-for-mage?p=1031831#post1031831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Euthanatos are going to have a big bone to pick with them due to their goals clashing hard with their 8 spoked wheel, the Chodona. Immortality denies Kala, the belief that all things will and must decay in time, and return to the other side of the cycle. While Gopaya compels them to act against anything which may corrupt the cycle of Death and Rebirth.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThey are probably gonna be more pissed when they discover that not only is this Nephandi thing but that the mundane founder is actually Hindi. Also, would that mean they would be the most likely mage group to assassinate executives and board members?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T15:11:29-08:00","id":1031840,"title":"","content":"Wanna give it an interesting twist?.<br /> <br /> make it one of the companies that run under the Special Division category in tecnocracy.<br /> <br /> LONG STORY SHORT..Are you familiar with werewolf? then skip to the end<br /> <br /> If Not: here it goes.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aYAJopwEYv8\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aYAJopwEYv8\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aYAJopwEYv8\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aYAJopwEYv8 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> Somehow Nephandi joined the technocracy and they been working out inside of it for decades. Helping the development of Pentex through tecnology and what not.<br /> What is Pentex you Ask? a massive multinational company that has half of the world on its pockets, working for &quot;A Greener Tomorrow, Today!.&quot; whats the catch? Pentex works For The Wyrm *Quoe Dramatic Music*. So, how did the all powerful technocracy allowed the existance of such devious group? well.. they didn't.<br /> Basically, due the final days of the Week of Nightmares, everything went AWOL and the agents lost contact with the Head HQ Known as Control.<br /> <br /> Once the technocracy lost contact with control, every cell started to go independent by being blindly guided by the Precepts of Damian , a series of Laws that every operative must follow (Brush your teeths, dont eat after midnight, dont do deals with the draculas , protect and serve kind of deal)<br /> <br /> The Technocracy pulled a &quot;Captain America: The Winter Soldier / Civil War.&quot; and there was a Civil War (No, No chris evans in this one), Why ? because if you blindly follow the orders of an invisible dictator in the sky, its easy to start missunderstand his words, and when some other mad zelot comes saying &quot;Hey, this law doesnt make any sense.&quot; or &quot;I think i understand it better than you.&quot; Well... <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYSYASpNiw\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4kYSYASpNiw</a> .<br /> While every cell was recovering, the $yndicate discovered that some of the budget went to Special Projects Division. Once they started to settle the paperwork they saw that they had a connection to pentex....And Pentex is Fucking Evil.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy went Haywire..Again (Dramatization: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DrQcNwsjVEQ\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DrQcNwsjVEQ</a> ) , and they proceed on a second civil war within the civil war (Warception!) To eradicate every single nasty Nephandi within the group. but the damage was already done, the patents of the Unions equipment was already in Pentex hands. It was too little too late.. and to add insult to injury, Pentex (anonymously) kept sending Checks to the technocracy with a &quot;Thanks Lololol. U Mad Bro?&quot; and a lot of cash based on the products that they were making with Technocratic Equipment.<br /> Have Fun.<br /> <br /> So yeah..Special Divisions before the Civil War.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 01-14-2017, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T15:44:18-08:00","id":1031855,"title":"","content":"Good stuff up there.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Euthanatos are going to have a big bone to pick with them due to their goals clashing hard with their 8 spoked wheel, the Chodona. Immortality denies Kala, the belief that all things will and must decay in time, and return to the other side of the cycle. While Gopaya compels them to act against anything which may corrupt the cycle of Death and Rebirth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, Immortality isn't going to ring well among them. Nor among mages that think that Immortality it's unnatural (like the Verbena), or shouldn't be granted to the non-enlightened (like the Hermetics). Neither with those Choristers that think that dying and going to the afterlife it's important.<br /> <br /> Also, the Technocracy knows perfectly well that true immortality it's as Vulgar as Vulgar can get. So, either they will believe it's all bullshit to promote their product, or that they're dangerous.<br /> The Technocracy also knows that the only way to create perfect clones, so perfect that they can replace people it's impossible without enlightened or deviant means. So, if the company isn't one of them, then they're going to investigate it troughly, and shut it down if they find the smallest thing to complain about.<br /> On the other hand, if it's from them, they also have reasons to investigate &amp; shut it down, because Paradox it's ilegal. This company isn't respecting the Time Table, and it's a heavy security risk, so unless it's protected by a very big shot in the Technocracy, it's going to be seen as an enemy.<br /> If it's protected by a big shot, however, bold non corrupt agents , might try to use the Traditions as a way to deal with them. Giving information, and weak spots of the company to them in hope they will act like the terrorists that they are, and demolish that dangerous business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T16:05:10-08:00","id":1031861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1031436-advice-on-a-antagonist-idea-for-mage?p=1031855#post1031855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good stuff up there.<br /> <br /> Yea, Immortality isn't going to ring well among them. Nor among mages that think that Immortality it's unnatural (like the Verbena), or shouldn't be granted to the non-enlightened (like the Hermetics). Neither with those Choristers that think that dying and going to the afterlife it's important.<br /> <br /> Also, the Technocracy knows perfectly well that true immortality it's as Vulgar as Vulgar can get. So, either they will believe it's all bullshit to promote their product, or that they're dangerous.<br /> The Technocracy also knows that the only way to create perfect clones, so perfect that they can replace people it's impossible without enlightened or deviant means. So, if the company isn't one of them, then they're going to investigate it troughly, and shut it down if they find the smallest thing to complain about.<br /> On the other hand, if it's from them, they also have reasons to investigate &amp; shut it down, because Paradox it's ilegal. This company isn't respecting the Time Table, and it's a heavy security risk, so unless it's protected by a very big shot in the Technocracy, it's going to be seen as an enemy.<br /> If it's protected by a big shot, however, bold non corrupt agents , might try to use the Traditions as a way to deal with them. Giving information, and weak spots of the company to them in hope they will act like the terrorists that they are, and demolish that dangerous business.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, even the mundane founder knows they are kind of a long ways away from cloning a perfect human. But, that does not mean they aren't trying. Also, I came up with a twist for the cloning organs project. If they manage to create them they would sell them to hospitals and transplant patients. However, the Nephandi twist comes in when the organs start failing for no reason on certain days. When the pcs investigate, they figure out the company made the organs to expire on a certain date of their choosing so they could shake down more money from their clients.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T16:27:04-08:00","id":1031874,"title":"","content":"Well, cloning organs would be a seller, but it would require ten years of testing before the FDA approved of it. Of course, you could set up the clinic in the developing world, away from the attention of developed world regulators (and the majority of the Technocracy). If you want organs to be really horrible, bind a Bane into each organ, so the recipients will likely have to resist becoming a fomori. If they resist possession, the organ fails and the recipient needs another transplant (which gives the company more revenue and gives the company another opportunity to make wealthy people into fomori).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T16:32:26-08:00","id":1031878,"title":"","content":"That sounds fine and all. But, won't that drag them to W:TA? Unless, I can make them an enemy of both Mages and the Changing Breeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T17:25:27-08:00","id":1031894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1031436-advice-on-a-antagonist-idea-for-mage?p=1031878#post1031878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds fine and all. But, won't that drag them to W:TA? Unless, I can make them an enemy of both Mages and the Changing Breeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because something is possible, and even probable, doesn't mean it has to happen. You are allowed to limit the factions involved in your game for the sake of keeping things manageable. If the question arises of &quot;Why didn't X do something about this&quot; the answer can simply be &quot;They were busy with something else&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T17:41:22-08:00","id":1031897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1031436-advice-on-a-antagonist-idea-for-mage?p=1031894#post1031894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just because something is possible, and even probable, doesn't mean it has to happen. You are allowed to limit the factions involved in your game for the sake of keeping things manageable. If the question arises of &quot;Why didn't X do something about this&quot; the answer can simply be &quot;They were busy with something else&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Also, here is one of Genesis' executives<br /> <br /> James &quot; Fatty&quot; Robertson<br /> <br /> \u200bJames is a recent addition to Genesis' Board of Directors. He was elected to the Board after the death of Ravi Casmir, who was killed in a random stabbing by a lunatic who claimed he was messing with cosmic balance. Before being elected to the board, James oversaw the operations in Boston, not as a scientist however, but, as finance manager. As the company's new CFO James has access to the company's funding, which he uses to get rid of any &quot;opponents&quot; to the company's goal. Recently, he hired thugs to break up a protest at one of Genesis' labs.<br /> <br /> \u200bJames however, has a secret. He used to be a Irish mobster during the 60s, which gives him access to plenty of underworld contacts. His position in the mob was running a massive money laundering racket which was broken up by the feds in 1972. Fatty however, escaped the bust and was forced into hiding. In1995, he came out of hiding and took a job at Genesis. He knows the company's true agenda as a front for a Malfean mage, but he just doesn't a fuck.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat do you think of this guy. Could he be a threat to a coven of mages?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T18:09:16-08:00","id":1031902,"title":"","content":"Well first, we'll need to fill in some details. Because he's under an assumed identity and was part of organized crime, Fatty probably had plastic surgery done to change his face. Any number of plot points could arise from this, from the question of where his plastic surgeon is, to whether the government has his fingerprints or DNA on file. But these are small potatoes, and don't need to come into play if you don't want them.<br /> <br /> Next, we need to establish what, exactly, Fatty knows. Sure, he might have an idea about his boss's true nature, but I doubt it goes much beyond &quot;an idea&quot;. Mages are under no obligation to reveal themselves to the ones working for them, and followers of dark powers are most secretive. Fatty could be aware that his boss has power - supernatural power - but not know the full extent of that power, nor its source. It depends on what his boss chooses to share, and I suspect he'd share little. From Fatty's perspective, this is a double-edged sword. He knows his boss has resources above and beyond what is normally possible (and thus can be tapped for a little help). But he also knows that said boss can turn said resources on him, if Fatty is uncooperative or incompetent. And if Fatty thinks his boss is more powerful than he really is, the CFO may commit to plans of action that assume access to that power, leaving them all in a tight position. The classic risk of underlings overestimating one's abilities.<br /> <br /> If Fatty is smart, he'll realize that his ignorance of his boss's true strength could bite him if the CFO isn't careful. He'd also realize that asking said boss for help over every little problem can make him seem weak or incompetent. As such, if he's clever (and a mob veteran who lasted for any length of time should be at least a little clever), he'll try to use as much of his own resources to solve his problems, relying on his boss as little as possible. Those resources, of course, are money, underlings, and connections. How he uses those depends on his personality. An aggressive person might try to attack his problems directly. A more subtle person might use indirect means. It's the difference between sending thugs to attack the coven, and sending spies to dig up intel and dirt on them. One that tries to remain above board on problems might attempt to use the legal system and press to work for him, playing the victim in any conflicts (while trying to make sure none of the company's incriminating activities get out).<br /> <br /> How much he knows about his boss will also inform how much he can guess as to the capabilities of the PCs. What he thinks they can do informs his defenses and strategies. If he knows that Mages can go invisible, he might equip his people with infrared goggles. If he knows they can influence men's minds, he might work to grab strong-willed people, or else have everyone work in pairs (lowering the chances the PCs have to isolate and manipulate). Try to come up with a list of specific powers Fatty knows or suspects Mages to be capable of, and update it as the PCs tackle his operations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T18:19:57-08:00","id":1031905,"title":"","content":"Well, Pentex was created by the Syndicate, so the Technocracy is already hip deep with the largest creator of fomori in the world. Since you are thinking of using a Malfean Nephandi anyway, you are going to be dealing with Banes and Fomori because the Nephandi is worshiping the Wyrm. Quite frankly though, unless your Nephandi does something outrageously stupid, he should fly under the radar of the Garou because, quite frankly, the Garou have bigger fish to fry (the Weaver and the Wyrm). There are probably millions of fomori in the world (I use a 1:2,500 proportion for the number of human fomori myself) so another few hundred fomori are not going to be noticed by the Garou. In fact, the only people who are probably going to notice are Infernal Mages and Infernal Sorcerers who were planning to recruit the desperate and wealthy people into the Demon worshiping crowd for the benefit of their patrons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T20:45:11-08:00","id":1031964,"title":"","content":"Fatty could definitely know about his boss' power. But, he does not know how exactly he got them. Him knowing about the Wyrm is debatable. He sure does act like your average Wyrm-tainted businessman. But, he has no idea about the formori the company has in it's labs or the BSDs his &quot;magical&quot; boss hired. Also, Fatty wouldn't attack the pcs in person. He would probably hire thugs to fight them for him. If confronted, Fatty would most likely try to flee, resulting in a chase scene. Also, he has a list he calls &quot; his personal journal&quot;, which include every power he thinks a mage could have. From flinging fire balls all the way to pulling rabbits out of their hats. Also, Fatty's operations are mostly gonna be financial institutions. Like, one story can have you heist money out of the company's bank account. Fatty spends most of his time in Boston, hanging out at his favorite pub, &quot; The Drunken Bastard&quot; or in his office, analyzing company assets. He is also a gourmet, he has been know to eat at many restaurants, his favorite being a little Indian restaurant he goes to whenever a business trip takes him to California.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T02:56:42-08:00","id":1032061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1031436-advice-on-a-antagonist-idea-for-mage?p=1031442#post1031442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another, more subtle use, would be to make sure that all the clones are partially related to one individual. This, therefore, would mean they all share a Sympathetic (and therefore Correspondence) connection to a person in the Nephandus' control, if it isn't the Nephandus himself (though I doubt the Fallen would risk that same bond of Contagion being used against them). Suddenly, he has a legion of individuals that are predisposed towards being controlled by him magickally. Agents positioned in many places throughout society, susceptible to mind control or other Effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you make the Nephandi a K'llasshaa, you could make it so the Nephandus sees himself as the head of octopus (or some other lifeform), and the clones, or people with artificially grown organs, as tentacles or pseudopods. Or he could see himself as a tentacle of an Outer Lord, and the people as his sensory organs, suckers etc. This is accomplished with some technepandic (or outright mystic) ritual; for example by putting something like the Yellow Sign on the clones or organs. This is his Correspondence, and wherever the tentacles are, he can scry, co-locate, create portals and use other Spheres. So if a tentacle touches someone he can use Prime (including vampirism); if a tentacle speaks to someone, this channels Mind; contorting into weird and unnatural shapes enables Entropy; self-mutilation, tattoos and scarring channel Correspondence (portals would be major body horror). Level 5 effects could be used if there are several tentacles in an area.<br /> <br /> The people used for this may or might not be aware of what is happening. They might have a fugue state (for a few seconds or whole hours) when they are speaking lovecraftian phrases and contorting in weird shapes so that effects can be cast through them; or they might have an urge to touch someone while being aware of it, but not knowing why. This might necessitate Mind used along with Correspondence. Perhaps they could slowly be made into (un)willing Acolytes; and then Mind wouldn't be needed.<br /> <br /> Trying to use this against the Nephandus would be risky, as the Nephandus can sense any tentacle which is somehow tampered with, and can channel effects at those attempting to use tentacles against him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1031436-advice-on-a-antagonist-idea-for-mage?p=1031463#post1031463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another possibility would be for the Mage to be an Infernal Technocrat instead of a Nephandi. He would be secretly using Dark Technology to create clones that will be inclined to sin in the fashion associated with his patron.</div> </div> </div> </div>This can be the case for a Malfean Nephandi as well - the Urge-Wyrms and the Majelin Incarna are associated with emotions and concepts. So clones consecrated to Lady Aife could be creating pain cults etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-15-2017, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T07:38:42-08:00","id":1032122,"title":"","content":"Thanks for helping out so far. I had decided to make the Nephandi a Malfean one. Would a Malfean hire a BSD? If so, I am thinking of including one as either the Head of Genesis' Security Forces or as a board member. Also, The Genesis Board of Directors is multi-national. They come from every continent Genesis has locations in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T08:22:47-08:00","id":1032138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1031436-advice-on-a-antagonist-idea-for-mage?p=1032122#post1032122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Would a Malfean hire a BSD?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they both go through the Black Spiral. It's noted that other Nephandi find it disturbing that Malfeans hang out with Black Spirals. However, Black Spirals can be very untrustworthy and self-interested, putting themselves and/or their Tribe first. If the Nephandus and Black Spirals serve different aspects of the Wyrm it might also impact their cooperation negatively.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T09:54:54-08:00","id":1032180,"title":"","content":"BSDs are more mercenaries that you hire for specific jobs rather than people you hire permanently. I would suggest a Fomori Sorcerer for the Chief Security Officer (I generally offer Sorcerer characters the option to purchase Possessed as a 5 point Merit). Just create them using either the rules in Sorcerer: Hedge Wizard or Sorcerer: Revised (depending on which version you like for your Mage games), purchase the Possessed Merit for them, and give them the desired Powers and Taints from Possessed. You could have the rest of the security force being Fomori as well if you wish, since you are a Malfean Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T09:59:47-08:00","id":1032185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1031436-advice-on-a-antagonist-idea-for-mage?p=1032180#post1032180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BSDs are more mercenaries that you hire for specific jobs rather than people you hire permanently. I would suggest a Fomori Sorcerer for the Chief Security Officer (I generally offer Sorcerer characters the option to purchase Possessed as a 5 point Merit). Just create them using either the rules in Sorcerer: Hedge Wizard or Sorcerer: Revised (depending on which version you like for your Mage games), purchase the Possessed Merit for them, and give them the desired Powers and Taints from Possessed. You could have the rest of the security force being Fomori as well if you wish, since you are a Malfean Nephandi.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah, I can see a formori being a security chief working out better than BSD. Also, the Board would probably end up using formori as bodyguards. Especially if the traditions or Technocracy find out about them. Also, the next board member I will describe will either be a guy with split personalities or a old scientist who is paralyzed from the waist down. Which one would you like to hear about first?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T19:44:32-08:00","id":1032438,"title":"","content":"Say hello to board member number 2<br /> <br /> Alex Wilks<br /> <br /> \u200bMr. Wilks seems like your average white-collar businessman. He is in charge of Genesis marketing department and is a member of their Board of Directors. What no one knows is that Alex is hiding a dark secret. He is only one of two personalities. His second personality is Bill Johnson, a sadistic man who has been known to beat the shit out of anyone who crosses him. Alex tries to keep Bill repressed while Bill tries to come out more often. This isn't helped by the stress that working as a marketing director brings and Bill has been slipping out more and more. Alex thinks no one knows his secret, but he is wrong. The Malfean in charge of the company is aware of this second personality and is trying everything he can to make Bill the dominate personality.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:06:29-08:00","id":1032813,"title":"","content":"Who do you guys like more? Wilks or Robertson?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}